            ":question/worked-solution": "Let's solve this using the general formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{1}{1+2x}+\\frac{1}{1-2x})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{1+2x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{1-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1-2x|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{1+2x}{1-2x}|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡K \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(K|\\frac{1+2x}{1-2x}|)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we used the laws of logarithms to write the result as a single logarithm."
